---
title: Recipe Name
# introduction: short blurb shown under the title
# servings: 4          # number only; shown as "Serves 4"
# yield: 800%grams     # how much it makes (number%unit); lets other recipes ask for e.g. @./this{400%grams}
tags:
  - entres  # one of: entres, sides, desserts, breakfast, condiment, ingredient
source:
  name: Site Name
  url: https://www.any-site.com/
---

-- Comments start with -- or can be [- inline -].
-- Blank line = new step.
--
-- @name{qty%unit}(note)   ingredient, e.g. @chicken{2%lbs}(cut into pieces)
-- @salt{}                 ingredient with no quantity
-- @?cocoa powder{1%tbsp}  optional ingredient (listed separately)
-- @./pie-dough{400%grams} link to another recipe; a unit needs a matching yield in that recipe
-- #baking sheet{}         cookware
-- ~{10%minutes}           timer
-- = Section Name          starts a section (### heading)
-- > note text             a note rendered as a quote.
--
-- Use @ only on the first mention; later mentions are plain text.
-- Same name used with @ twice is summed, so keep names/case consistent.

= Section Name

Mix @ingredient{1%cup}(chopped) in a #large bowl{} for ~{5%minutes}.

> Optional note about the step above.
